From 2a6b5bf1daf769e8b71d3c5f66565d3318a15eb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac-build <b@steamac>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:01:55 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: diagnose command storage growth
 (STEAMAC-AK/AP/AN/AX)

The abort at IOGPUMetalCommandBufferStorageAllocResourceAtIndex+512 follows a NULL pooled-resource allocation on M1 Max/macOS 27.0.1; it is not the separate invalid resource-class assertion. Report 618cc727 grows from 52116 to 94944 MiB footprint while Metal resources stay near 3023 MiB. The retained reports cannot identify the missing memory owner.

Expose real allocator heap and residency usage, with snapshots before encoder creation/end and recording end. Report per-Metal-buffer encoder attempts separately from Vulkan recording counts, uploads, large buffers and cached pool object counts. Normal reports use doubling high waters; cbs logs each recording. Preserve allocator lifetimes: executable siblings can share an allocator and resetting one would invalidate the other.

Private M1 Max component build and command-allocator regression pass: 85 explicit snapshots, 3 bounded growth snapshots. After warmup, 64 rounds stay at 55825760 bytes; 1024 render/fill pairs with two executable siblings plateau at 735663456 bytes over repeated recordings. The old driver fails only the new diagnostic assertions; its allocations also plateau. Exact game abort not reproduced, so no speculative allocator fix.
